<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 15 September, from 1776 to 1950.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1776</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British troops land at Kip's Bay and take New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a heavy naval bombardment, British forces landed on Manhattan at Kip's Bay, sending American troops fleeing. New York stayed in British hands until 1783.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1830</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Liverpool and Manchester Railway opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first inter-city railway relying wholly on steam locomotives opened with great ceremony. The day was marred when the MP William Huskisson was struck and killed by Stephenson's Rocket.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1835</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Beagle reaches the Galápagos Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Darwin spent five weeks studying the islands' finches, tortoises and mockingbirds. His observations later helped shape his theory of evolution by natural selection.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1916</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tanks go into battle for the first time on the Somme</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British Mark I tanks supported an attack at Flers-Courcelette. Many broke down, but those that advanced showed the potential of armoured warfare.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1940</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The RAF repels massed daylight raids on Battle of Britain Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Luftwaffe launched two huge raids on London and lost around 60 aircraft. Two days later Hitler postponed his planned invasion of Britain indefinitely.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1950</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UN forces land at Inchon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines led General MacArthur's amphibious landing at Inchon, far behind North Korean lines. Seoul was retaken within two weeks and the North Korean army collapsed.</p></li></ol>
